---
layout: layouts/base.njk
permalink: /subscribe/
title: Subscribe
---
<article class="article page-article">
  {%- if site.subscribe_embed_code %}
  {#- The sign-up form from Kit carries its own headline and description,
      so the page doesn't repeat them. Edit that wording in Kit. #}
  <h1 class="visually-hidden">Subscribe to the Boxborough News newsletter</h1>
  <div class="subscribe-panel subscribe-panel-embed">
    {{ site.subscribe_embed_code | safe }}
  </div>
  {%- else %}
  <header class="article-head">
    <h1 class="article-title">Get Boxborough News every Friday</h1>
  </header>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>Our free email newsletter arrives every Friday with the week's town news, features, and upcoming events. You can unsubscribe at any time, and we never share your email address.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="subscribe-panel">
    <a class="button button-large" href="{{ site.subscribe_url }}">Sign up for the free newsletter</a>
    {%- if "docs.google.com/forms" in site.subscribe_url %}
    <p class="small">The sign-up form opens in Google Forms. Just enter your email address. You don't need to sign in to Google.</p>
    {%- endif %}
  </div>
  {%- endif %}
  <div class="prose">
    {%- if collections.latestIssue %}
    <p><a href="/newsletter/latest/">See a recent email</a> (the {{ collections.latestIssue.date | date("long") }} issue) to get a sense of what you'll receive.</p>
    {%- endif %}
    <p>Prefer a feed reader? Follow our <a href="/feed.xml">RSS feed</a>. You can also find us on {% if site.facebook_url %}<a href="{{ site.facebook_url }}">Facebook</a>{% endif %}{% if site.instagram_url %} and <a href="{{ site.instagram_url }}">Instagram</a>{% endif %}.</p>
  </div>
</article>
